{"node_id": "real_049_MedlinePlus-Magazine-2024-Issue1_12_HY_009", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0019"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0019_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Tezepelumab is a type of medication called a monoclonal\nantibody. Monoclonal antibodies are immune proteins made\nin a lab to target specific diseases or conditions in the body.\nTezepelumab works by blocking specific signals between the\ncells that cause allergic inflammation and typical allergic\nreactions such as itching, sneezing, and runny nose. In other\nwords, it helps relieve allergy symptoms by targeting the source.", "semantic_text": "Tezepelumab is a type of medication called a monoclonal antibody. Monoclonal antibodies are immune proteins made in a lab to target specific diseases or conditions in the body. Tezepelumab works by blocking specific signals between the cells that cause allergic inflammation and typical allergic reactions such as itching, sneezing, and runny nose. In other words, it helps relieve allergy symptoms by targeting the source.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0019_geometry", "bbox": [632, 872, 1134, 1053], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0019"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_2/hybrid/real_049_MedlinePlus-Magazine-2024-Issue1/page_0012/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_049_MedlinePlus-Magazine-2024-Issue1_12_HY_010", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0020"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0020_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Scientists are still studying tezepelumab. They want to know\nhow the drug works inside our cells. This could help scientists\nbetter understand what's happening at the cellular level, leading\nto even more effective allergy treatments in the future.", "semantic_text": "Scientists are still studying tezepelumab. They want to know how the drug works inside our cells. This could help scientists better understand what's happening at the cellular level, leading to even more effective allergy treatments in the future.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0020_geometry", "bbox": [632, 1056, 1137, 1157], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0020"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_2/hybrid/real_049_MedlinePlus-Magazine-2024-Issue1/page_0012/decisions.json"}
